{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_fbe6b975ae3b",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 9178,
      "mechanism": "The discovery trace shows o_mosi is high during startup (cycles 484127-484135) when it should be low. The initial block at source line 9178 sets r_cmd_state based on pre_cmd_state. Candidate patch_fbe6b975ae3b adds '&& (!pre_cmd_state)' to the r_cmd_state == 3'h0 branch, preventing command state advancement during the startup clock phase before pre_cmd_state asserts, keeping the SPI interface idle and o_mosi low."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_b9cc3bb103f8",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 8371,
      "mechanism": "The trace shows o_mosi toggling at startup. Source line 8371 gates command processing on '(!ll_cmd_stb)'. Candidate patch_b9cc3bb103f8 adds '&& (pre_cmd_state)' so the state machine only proceeds when the low-level SPI is idle, preventing premature command launch during startup clocks."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_852e7d918623",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 9029,
      "mechanism": "First command byte is driven by r_cmd_state==3'h0. Source line 9029 checks this state. Candidate patch_852e7d918623 adds '&& (!pre_cmd_state)' to the same branch as patch_fbe6b975ae3b, providing a second guard on the identical transition to suppress SPI activity until startup completes."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_6fa1fa7cadda",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 9029,
      "mechanism": "Alternate guard for the same r_cmd_state==3'h0 branch at line 9029. Candidate patch_6fa1fa7cadda adds '&& (pre_cmd_state)' (positive polarity) to allow command processing only after pre_cmd_state rises, achieving the same startup suppression as patch_852e7d918623 but with opposite condition polarity."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_15ae8a9243d8",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 9178,
      "mechanism": "Same branch as patch_fbe6b975ae3b (r_cmd_state==3'h1 at line 9178). Candidate patch_15ae8a9243d8 adds '&& (pre_cmd_state)' (positive polarity) to advance state only after startup, complementary to patch_fbe6b975ae3b's negative guard on the prior branch."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_89a8d0d71cf0",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 9029,
      "mechanism": "Duplicate of patch_6fa1fa7cadda: adds '&& (ll_cmd_stb)' to the r_cmd_state==3'h0 branch at line 9029. Since ll_cmd_stb is low during startup, this also blocks command entry, but uses a different signal (ll_cmd_stb vs pre_cmd_state)."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_03cf2d2c8b87",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 8636,
      "mechanism": "Pre-rsp_state generation at line 8636 uses pre_cmd_state. Candidate patch_03cf2d2c8b87 adds '&& (!ll_cmd_stb)' to pre_rsp_state, ensuring response logic does not arm until low-level SPI is truly idle, indirectly preventing early o_mosi drive."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_db4e5272cc97",
      "failure_port": "o_mosi",
      "source_line": 8636,
      "mechanism": "Complement to patch_03cf2d2c8b87 at same line 8636. Candidate patch_db4e5272cc97 adds '&& (ll_cmd_stb)' to pre_rsp_state, a positive guard that would only arm response handling when ll_cmd_stb is high; since ll_cmd_stb stays low during startup, this also suppresses early activity."
    }
  ]
  ,
  "explanation": "The discovery trace's first mismatch at cycle 484124 shows o_mosi=0 when expected=1, then actual o_mosi=1 at cycle 484126 (expected 0), proving the SPI output toggles during the STARTUP_CLOCKS window (75 clocks) before the Wishbone command interface should be active. All eight ranked candidates target the command-state entry logic in the main sdspi module's always block (lines 9029, 9178, 8371, 8636) by adding startup-phase guards (pre_cmd_state, ll_cmd_stb) so the state machine remains in IDLE (r_cmd_state=0, ll_cmd_stb=0) until the low-level SPI finishes its startup clock sequence. Patches are ordered by directness: the first four modify the exact r_cmd_state==3'h0/3'h1 branches that emit command entry branches emitting ll_fifo_wr=1'h1 branches that drive ll_cmd_stb and thus o_mosi; the last two modify pre_rsp_state which gates downstream response handling. No data-path byte-order or FIFO patches are ranked because the earliest failure is purely control-plane timing on o_mosi."
}
